                            <div class="faq">
                                            <div class="mb-10">
                            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Dates en programme</h2>
                            <div class="divide-y divide-fuchsia-medium">
                                                                    <div id="faq-77" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-77" data-faq-toggle>
            When does Dutch Design Week (DDW) take place?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-77" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">DDW takes place from Saturday 17 to Sunday 25 October 2026.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-9" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-9" data-faq-toggle>
            Where can I find the DDW programme?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-9" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">View the full programme, including all projects and participating designers,</span> <u style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 255);"><a href="https://ddw.nl/nl/programma?_gl=1*4wonjf*_gcl_au*NjI2NjEzOTc0LjE3Nzk4MDQ3Mjg.*_ga*MTE2NzgzODAwMC4xNzU2MTA4NTUw*_ga_F73HVBVWKB*czE3ODYwMjAzMjUkbzI3MSRnMSR0MTc4NjAyMTM0NiRqNjAkbDAkaDA." rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a></u> <span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">on the programme page.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-39" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-39" data-faq-toggle>
            Is there a special programme for children and young people?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-39" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Yes. DDW Young brings together projects from the programme that are particularly interesting for children and young people aged 6 to 18. View the DDW Young &amp; Education programme</span><a href="https://ddw.nl/nl/ddw-young?_gl=1*ze213v*_gcl_au*NjI2NjEzOTc0LjE3Nzk4MDQ3Mjg.*_ga*MTE2NzgzODAwMC4xNzU2MTA4NTUw*_ga_F73HVBVWKB*czE3ODYwMjAzMjUkbzI3MSRnMSR0MTc4NjAyMTM0NiRqNjAkbDAkaDA." rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://ddw.nl/en/main-menu-programme/ddw-young-education" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a></u><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-8" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-8" data-faq-toggle>
            Can I participate in DDW26?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-8" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">The call for entries for the upcoming edition of DDW is currently closed.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                            </div>
                        </div>
                                            <div class="mb-10">
                            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Locations and Opening Hours</h2>
                            <div class="divide-y divide-fuchsia-medium">
                                                                    <div id="faq-40" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-40" data-faq-toggle>
            Where does Dutch Design Week take place?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-40" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">DDW takes place at dozens of locations across Eindhoven. Check </span><a href="https://ddw.nl/en/map" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">the map</a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> to see which exhibitions, projects and activities can be found at each location.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-41" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-41" data-faq-toggle>
            What are the opening hours of DDW locations?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-41" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Most locations are open daily from 11:00 to 18:00. Some locations have different opening hours, so please check the latest information in</span><a href="https://ddw.nl/nl/programma?_gl=1*1ulcxzo*_gcl_au*NjI2NjEzOTc0LjE3Nzk4MDQ3Mjg.*_ga*MTE2NzgzODAwMC4xNzU2MTA4NTUw*_ga_F73HVBVWKB*czE3ODYwMjAzMjUkbzI3MSRnMSR0MTc4NjAyMTM0NiRqNjAkbDAkaDA." rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://ddw.nl/nl/programma?_gl=1*1ulcxzo*_gcl_au*NjI2NjEzOTc0LjE3Nzk4MDQ3Mjg.*_ga*MTE2NzgzODAwMC4xNzU2MTA4NTUw*_ga_F73HVBVWKB*czE3ODYwMjAzMjUkbzI3MSRnMSR0MTc4NjAyMTM0NiRqNjAkbDAkaDA." rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">the programme</a></u><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> before your visit.</span></p><p>Please note: o<span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">n the first Saturday, the Design Academy Eindhoven Graduation Show opens at 13:00.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-43" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-43" data-faq-toggle>
            Can I leave a location and return later?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-43" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Yes. As long as you are wearing a valid DDW wristband, you can leave and return to ticketed locations during opening hours. Please keep in mind that locations can be busy and you may need to queue again.</span></p><p><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Please note: </strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Your wristband is valid once it has been secured around your wrist. If you remove or cut it off yourself, it will no longer be valid. You cannot collect a wristband on behalf of someone else.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-42" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-42" data-faq-toggle>
            Are cloakrooms or lockers available?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-42" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">No, most DDW locations do not have cloakrooms or lockers.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                            </div>
                        </div>
                                            <div class="mb-10">
                            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Tickets</h2>
                            <div class="divide-y divide-fuchsia-medium">
                                                                    <div id="faq-10" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-10" data-faq-toggle>
            Where can I buy a ticket for Dutch Design Week?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-10" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Tickets are available via the </span><u style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 255);"><a href="https://ddw.nl/en/tickets" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">ticket page</a></u><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">. There you will also find information about ticket types, prices, points of sale and access to the different locations.</span></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">During DDW, you can also purchase tickets at the door at:</span></p><ul><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Klokgebouw</span></li><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Design Academy Eindhoven Graduation Show</span></li><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Building TX</span></li><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Sectie-C</span></li><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Eindhoven Central Station</span></li><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Van Abbemuseum</span></li></ul><p></p><p><u style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Good to know</u></p><ul><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">At physical ticket points, payment is by debit or credit card only. Cash payments are not accepted.</span></li><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">The family ticket is only available at the door for a fixed price of €88.00. The entire family must be present at the ticket desk when collecting the ticket.</span></li></ul>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-48" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-48" data-faq-toggle>
            What is included with a DDW ticket?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-48" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">During DDW, you can exchange your e-ticket for a personal wristband. This gives you access to all ticketed locations throughout the nine days of DDW:</span></p><ul><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">Klokgebouw</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">Graduation Show DAE</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">Van Abbemuseum</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">Sectie-C</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">Kazerne </span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">New Order of Fashion </span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">Dutch Invertuals</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">Forward Furniture exhibition on Strijp TX</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">&#39;HUB Bouw aan morgen&#39;, BioBased creations op de Caai</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">Designing Society</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">De Kruisruimte </span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">Building TT </span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(29, 28, 29); background-color: transparent;">&#39;Young Graduates HUB&#39;, DDW x Design Perron (previously VGZ building) </span></li></ul><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">All other DDW locations are free to visit and do not require a ticket. </span></p><p>With a valid DDW wristband and registration, you can use the <strong>Polestar Design Rides</strong>. They operate daily from 11:00 to 18:00 between all official DDW locations. <a href="https://www.polestar.com/nl/engage/ddw26-design-rides/?campaignId=2026_NL_ddw26designrides" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">You can register here</a>. A wristband is required to use the Polestar Design Rides, but registration is not mandatory.</p><p><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Please note: </strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Your wristband is valid once it has been secured around your wrist. If you remove or cut it off yourself, it will no longer be valid. You cannot collect a wristband on behalf of someone else.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-53" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-53" data-faq-toggle>
            How much does a DDW ticket cost?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-53" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">To 10 October, the following rates apply:</span></p><ul><li><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Regular ticket: € 29,50</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Youth and student ticket: € 17,50</span></li></ul><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">From 11 October, the following rates apply:</span></p><ul><li><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Regular ticket: € 32,50</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Youth and student ticket: € 19,50</span></li></ul><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Or purchase a ticket for a single location.</span></p><p></p><p><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Good to know</strong></p><ul><li><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Children aged 11 and under can visit DDW free of charge.</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">All prices include VAT and service fees.</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Your ticket confirmation email contains a button that allows you to download your VAT invoice. Please note that the details on the invoice cannot be changed after your ticket has been purchased.</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Your wristband is valid once it has been secured around your wrist. If you remove or cut it off yourself, it will no longer be valid. You cannot collect a wristband on behalf of someone else.</span></li></ul>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-106" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-106" data-faq-toggle>
            Can I buy a ticket for a single location?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-106" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Single-location tickets are available for a limited number of locations:</span></p><ul><li><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/iYbQ1PvnYtMnNB4EA" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Dutch Invertuals</a>: <span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">€5,00</span></li><li><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/5xkBNYT8CiheWuJa7" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Kazerne</a>: €5,00</li><li><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/o1ueWLzVdQUXqseW7" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">New Order of Fashion</a>: €2,50</li><li><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/TQwKBXp9FABZ2bLZ8" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Next Nature / Evoluon</a>: regular museum ticket</li><li><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/6saYqkhiQKEFNLa38" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Philips Museum</a>: regular museum ticket</li><li><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/NYMw1AgU6HM1fQ4F7" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Van Abbemuseum</a>: regular museum ticket</li></ul><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">For all other ticketed locations, you will need a regular DDW ticket.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-76" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-76" data-faq-toggle>
            Where can I go if I have another question about tickets?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-76" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">View the </span><u style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://s3.amazonaws.com/ddw2025test/downloads/files/o1fHjhRprk6rmNSSViJ8tSLrSzfLOHXC1PETS87G.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">ticket and admission terms and conditions</a></u><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">, visit the </span><u style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://app-api.ddw.nl/nl/tickets" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">ticket page</a></u><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> or consult the </span><u style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://ddw.nl/plan-je-bezoek?_gl=1*rj6n0w*_gcl_au*NjI2NjEzOTc0LjE3Nzk4MDQ3Mjg.*_ga*MTE2NzgzODAwMC4xNzU2MTA4NTUw*_ga_F73HVBVWKB*czE3ODYwMjc0MDQkbzI3MyRnMSR0MTc4NjAyODUzOCRqMzkkbDAkaDA." rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">visitor information page</a></u><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Can&#39;t find the answer to your question? Email </span><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255); background-color: transparent;"><a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="ea9e8389818f9e99aa8e9f9e89828e8f99838d848c859f848e8b9e838584c4898587">[email&#160;protected]</a></span><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-82" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-82" data-faq-toggle>
            Is there a reduced rate for visitors on a limited budget?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-82" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Dutch Design Foundation (DDF) works with Cultuur Inclusief to make DDW accessible to more people. Each year, 500 tickets are available through</span><a href="https://www.cultuur-inclusief.nl/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> </a><u style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 255);"><a href="https://www.cultuur-inclusief.nl/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Cultuur Inclusief</a></u><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> for €2.50 for people who are unable to pay the regular ticket price. Would you like to purchase one of these tickets? You can apply from 1 September via the</span><a href="https://www.cultuur-inclusief.nl/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> </a><u style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 255);"><a href="https://www.cultuur-inclusief.nl/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Cultuur Inclusief website</a></u><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">.</span></p><p><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Please note:</strong><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> Cultuur Inclusief manages a limited number of discount vouchers. Their website explains exactly who is eligible and how to apply. Dutch Design Foundation provides the discount but has no influence over the selection process or allocation of tickets.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                            </div>
                        </div>
                                            <div class="mb-10">
                            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Reachability</h2>
                            <div class="divide-y divide-fuchsia-medium">
                                                                    <div id="faq-36" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-36" data-faq-toggle>
            How do I get to Dutch Design Week?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-36" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Find all information about travelling to Eindhoven and getting between the different DDW locations</span><a href="https://ddw.nl/plan-your-visit/reachability?_gl=1*1ku58wq*_gcl_au*NjI2NjEzOTc0LjE3Nzk4MDQ3Mjg.*_ga*MTE2NzgzODAwMC4xNzU2MTA4NTUw*_ga_F73HVBVWKB*czE3ODYwMjU1NTMkbzI3MiRnMCR0MTc4NjAyNTU1MyRqNjAkbDAkaDA." rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> </a><u style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 255);"><a href="https://ddw.nl/plan-your-visit/reachability?_gl=1*1ku58wq*_gcl_au*NjI2NjEzOTc0LjE3Nzk4MDQ3Mjg.*_ga*MTE2NzgzODAwMC4xNzU2MTA4NTUw*_ga_F73HVBVWKB*czE3ODYwMjU1NTMkbzI3MiRnMCR0MTc4NjAyNTU1MyRqNjAkbDAkaDA." rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a></u><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-31" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-31" data-faq-toggle>
            How do I get there by bicycle?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-31" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>Cycling to Dutch Design Week is a great idea! Eindhoven has numerous bike paths that connect locations, and you can find free, and in some cases even supervised, bike parking.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-32" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-32" data-faq-toggle>
            How do I get there by train?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-32" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>If you travel to Dutch Design Week by train, you will arrive right in the heart of the design world. The intercity will take you to Eindhoven Central Station in the city centre. Local trains also stop at Strijp-S Station. Check the Journey Planner on ns.nl or the Reisplanner Xtra app from 10 days before your departure.</p><p></p><h2>NS Combi-Ticket</h2><p>This year, you can again use the NS Combi-Ticket. Are you coming to Dutch Design Week by train? Purchase your ticket through NS Spoordeelwinkel. If you are travelling by train from the Eindhoven region, check the special regional fare applicable to the NS Combi-Ticket.</p><p><a href="https://www.ns.nl/spoordeelwinkel" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Read more about the NS Combi-Ticket</a> →</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-34" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-34" data-faq-toggle>
            How do I get there by car?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-34" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>You can reach Eindhoven by car from Amsterdam/Utrecht via the A2, from Rotterdam/Tilburg via the A58, from Antwerp via the A67, and from Arnhem/Nijmegen via the A50.</p><p><a href="https://www.google.nl/maps/place/Eindhoven/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">View the route description</a> →</p><h2>P+R</h2><p>There are several parking garages at hotspots like the city centre and Strijp-S, but be aware that it can be busy. A good idea is to park at the various Park + Ride (P+R) locations: park on the outskirts of the city and take a direct bus to Dutch Design Week. There are two options:</p><ul><li><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/DYoiw3n4ZVGq5cYQ6" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">P+R Meerhoven</a>, on Noord-Brabantlaan</li><li>Bus connection to Strijp-S and Stationsplein locations</li><li><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/YnxYq3riG35AWSAf7" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">P+R Genneper Parken</a>, on Aalsterweg</li><li>Bus connection to Stationsplein</li></ul><p>Return bus tickets cost €0.50 per person.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-35" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-35" data-faq-toggle>
            How do I get there with coaching and busses?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-35" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>Large groups coming to Dutch Design Week by coach can use the Kiss &amp; Rides.</p><p>There are two clearly marked Kiss &amp; Ride locations, indicated by Dutch Design Week signs. One is at <a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/Yw9hQLZCbQ5a72TN7" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">the Flixbus stop</a> opposite the yellow bowling pins on John F. Kennedylaan, and the second is on <a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/zNpeCkeDSe56j5Q56" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Achtseweg Zuid</a>, on the other side of Beukenlaan, in Eindhoven.</p><p>At the Kiss &amp; Ride location at Achtseweg Zuid, the bus can temporarily park near Strijp-S Station for everyone to disembark. However, we urge you not to leave the bus there. There is ample free parking for coaches further along Achtseweg Zuid.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-38" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-38" data-faq-toggle>
            How do I travel between DDW locations?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-38" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">During DDW, there are several ways to travel around the city. Check </span><u style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 255);"><a href="https://ddw.nl/plan-your-visit/reachability?_gl=1*1ku58wq*_gcl_au*NjI2NjEzOTc0LjE3Nzk4MDQ3Mjg.*_ga*MTE2NzgzODAwMC4xNzU2MTA4NTUw*_ga_F73HVBVWKB*czE3ODYwMjU1NTMkbzI3MiRnMCR0MTc4NjAyNTU1MyRqNjAkbDAkaDA." rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a></u><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> for the latest information on routes and transport between locations.</span></p><p></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-75" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-75" data-faq-toggle>
            Can I use the Polestar Design Rides?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-75" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>You can use the Polestar Design Rides with a registration and a valid DDW wristband. The electric cars travel between all official DDW locations daily from 11.00 to 18.00. Please note: registering does not book or guarantee a Design Ride. It does not reserve a particular journey or departure time.</p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">There are designated </span>locations<span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> at:</span></p><ul><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Ketelhuisplein</span></li><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Piet Hein Eek</span></li><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Stadhuisplein</span></li><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Fuutlaan</span></li><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Design Academy Eindhoven</span></li><li><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Sectie-C</span></li></ul><p></p><p>Want to take a Polestar Design Ride from another DDW location? Call +31 (0)40 218 00 00. During busy periods or when it rains, a Design Ride may not be available straight away, so you may have to wait. You need a valid DDW wristband to ride.</p><p><a href="https://www.polestar.com/nl/engage/ddw26-design-rides/?campaignId=2026_NL_ddw26designrides" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">You can register here</a></p><p></p><p><em>*Please note: A wristband is required to use the Polestar Design Rides, but registration is not mandatory.</em></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-71" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-71" data-faq-toggle>
            Where can I find more information about reachability?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-71" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>All information regarding reachability to and at Dutch Design Week can be found <a href="https://ddw.nl/plan-your-visit/reachability" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a>.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                            </div>
                        </div>
                                            <div class="mb-10">
                            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Accessibility</h2>
                            <div class="divide-y divide-fuchsia-medium">
                                                                    <div id="faq-44" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-44" data-faq-toggle>
            Where can I find information about accessibility?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-44" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>All information regarding accessibility during Dutch Design Week can be found <a href="https://ddw.nl/plan-your-visit/accesibility" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a>.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-79" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-79" data-faq-toggle>
            Can I visit DDW in a wheelchair?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-79" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Accessibility varies by location. The programme provides up-to-date accessibility information for each location. More information about tickets and assistance can be found on the</span><a href="https://app-api.ddw.nl/nl/tickets" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> </a><u style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 255);"><a href="https://app-api.ddw.nl/nl/tickets" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">ticket page</a></u><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-45" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-45" data-faq-toggle>
            Are dogs allowed at Dutch Design Week?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-45" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>From September, you can check in the programme for each location whether dogs are allowed or not.</p><p>Service dogs are welcome everywhere. The dog must wear a harness clearly indicating that it&#39;s a service dog.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-61" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-61" data-faq-toggle>
            Is there a reduced rate for visitors on a limited budget?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-61" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Dutch Design Foundation (DDF) works with Cultuur Inclusief to make DDW accessible to more people. Each year, 500 tickets are available through</span><a href="https://www.cultuur-inclusief.nl/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://www.cultuur-inclusief.nl/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Cultuur Inclusief</a></u><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> for €2.50 for people who are unable to pay the regular ticket price. Would you like to purchase one of these tickets? You can apply from 1 September via the</span><a href="https://www.cultuur-inclusief.nl/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://www.cultuur-inclusief.nl/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Cultuur Inclusief website</a></u><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">.</span></p><p><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Please note:</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> Cultuur Inclusief manages a limited number of discount vouchers. Their website explains exactly who is eligible and how to apply. Dutch Design Foundation provides the discount but has no influence over the selection process or allocation of tickets.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-27" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-27" data-faq-toggle>
            What does the partnership with Cultuur Inclusief involve?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-27" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>If you are unable to buy a DDW ticket due to financial constraints, you can apply through the website of Cultuur Inclusief.</p><p>Cultuur Inclusief manages a limited number of discount vouchers for Dutch Design Week. You can read on their website how to qualify for a discount. We, as the organisers of Dutch Design Week, provide the tickets but have no say in the distribution of the discount vouchers.</p><p><a href="https://www.cultuur-inclusief.nl/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Read more on the Cultuur Inclusief website</a> →</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                            </div>
                        </div>
                                            <div class="mb-10">
                            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Frequently asked questions about Design Tours</h2>
                            <div class="divide-y divide-fuchsia-medium">
                                                                    <div id="faq-89" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-89" data-faq-toggle>
            Do you have a question about the Design Tours?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-89" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>Find the answer in the frequently asked questions below or contact us at <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#b7c3d8c2c5c4f7d3c2c3d4dfd3d2c4ded0d9d1d8c2d9d3d6c3ded8d999d4d8da" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="deaab1abacad9ebaabaabdb6babbadb7b9b0b8b1abb0babfaab7b1b0f0bdb1b3">[email&#160;protected]</span></a></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-92" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-92" data-faq-toggle>
            Where do the tours start?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-92" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>The tours start at the DDW Business Lounge in <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/place/Area+51+Eindhoven/@51.4481391,5.4534225,17z/data=!3m1!4b1!4m6!3m5!1s0x47c6d96af917b87d:0x210f6f62837cbfbe!8m2!3d51.4481391!4d5.4559974!16s%2Fm%2F027_nxf?entry=ttu" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Area51</a> on Ketelhuisplein. Mission Tours may also start at Fuutlaan. You will receive the exact starting location with your booking.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-93" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-93" data-faq-toggle>
            Until when can I book a tour?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-93" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>Custom Tours and Strijp-S Bites &amp; Insights can be booked until Friday 2 October inclusive. All other Design Tours can be booked until 19 October inclusive.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-90" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-90" data-faq-toggle>
            How do I book a Design Tour?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-90" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <h2>Via the Design Tours booking system:</h2><p><strong>Step 1</strong></p><ul><li>Choose one of the Design Tours. More information about the different tours can be found <a href="https://ddw.nl/nl/tours" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a>.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Step 2</strong></p><ul><li>Choose an available date and time slot and select the number of participants.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Step 3</strong></p><ul><li>A maximum of 15 people can join each tour. Are you booking for more than 15 people? You will automatically book multiple tours.</li></ul><h2></h2><h2>This is how it works in the booking system:</h2><ol><li>Enter the total number of participants in the form.</li><li>The system will show how many tours you need to accommodate everyone, initially within the same time slot.</li></ol><p></p><p><strong>Step 4</strong></p><ul><li>Select the language in which you would like to take the tour: Dutch or English.</li><li>Would you prefer another language? Email <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#295d465c5b5a694d5c5d4a414d4c5a404e474f465c474d485d404647074a4644" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="f2869d878081b2968786919a9697819b959c949d879c9693869b9d9cdc919d9f">[email&#160;protected]</span></a> and we will see whether we can accommodate your request.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Step 5</strong></p><ul><li>Add the tour booking to your basket.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Step 6</strong></p><ul><li>Check the summary of your selected tour. Is everything correct? Continue to the booking details.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Step 7</strong></p><ul><li>To prepare the quotation, we will ask for your contact details and reference number. You can also email the reference number to us later.</li></ul><p><em>Please note: make sure you enter the correct details in this form. These details will appear on the quotation and invoice.</em></p><p></p><p><strong>Step 8</strong></p><ul><li>Check the complete summary of your booking and confirm your booking.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Step 9</strong></p><ul><li>You will receive a quotation from us. You then have 14 days to accept it. The quotation includes a payment link. You will receive the invoice afterwards.</li></ul><p></p><p>Are you booking a Custom Tour? Once you have accepted the quotation, we will ask about your organisation’s areas of interest. Our team will use this information to create a tailored tour.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-100" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-100" data-faq-toggle>
            How much does a Design Tour cost?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-100" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>The price of each tour is listed alongside its description. When booking a tour, you also book admission tickets for Dutch Design Week (DDW). The cost is calculated based on the number of participants. These tickets are valid not only during the tour but throughout DDW, from Saturday 17 to Sunday 25 October.</p><p>Bicycle hire is charged separately for Mission Tours. For Strijp-S Bites &amp; Insights, additional costs per person apply for coffee and tea, lunch and drinks.</p><p>All prices shown exclude VAT. When you make a booking, you will receive a price overview that includes VAT.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-94" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-94" data-faq-toggle>
            How many people can join a tour?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-94" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>A maximum of 15 people can join each tour. Are you booking for more than 15 people? You will need to book multiple tours.</p><p>This is how it works in the booking system:</p><ul><li>Enter the total number of participants in the form.</li><li>The system will show how many tours you need to accommodate everyone, initially within the same time slot.</li><li>If that time slot is fully booked, the system will search for other available time slots for the remaining tours.</li></ul><h2></h2>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-91" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-91" data-faq-toggle>
            Which categories can you choose from?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-91" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>The tours are divided into three categories, with several options available within each category:</p><p><strong>Area Tours</strong></p><ul><li>Klokgebouw</li><li>Strijp-S</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Mission Tours</strong></p><ul><li>Thriving planet</li><li>Living environment</li><li>Health &amp; wellbeing</li><li>Equitable society</li><li>Digital futures</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Custom Tours</strong></p><p>Custom Tours are tailored to your organisation’s areas of interest and vary in length from 1.5 to 3 hours.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-95" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-95" data-faq-toggle>
            Have you already booked a tour, but would more people like to join?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-95" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>Additional participants can join, up to a maximum of 15 people per tour.</p><p>To add participants, purchase additional standard Dutch Design Week (DDW) tickets through the ticket shop. Make sure these tickets have been exchanged for DDW wristbands before the tour begins.</p><p>Please note: you must inform the Design Tours team about any additional participants so that sufficient technical equipment is available when the tour begins. Email <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#d7a3b8a2a5a497b3a2a3b4bfb3b2a4beb0b9b1b8a2b9b3b6a3beb8b9f9b4b8ba" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="097d667c7b7a496d7c7d6a616d6c7a606e676f667c676d687d606667276a6664">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>.</p><p>Additional participants can be registered until 14 October.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-96" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-96" data-faq-toggle>
            I booked a tour for more people than will be attending. Can I return the unused tickets?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-96" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>Unfortunately, tickets are non-refundable. Dutch Design Week runs for nine days and the tickets are transferable, so why not make a colleague, friend or family member happy with the remaining tickets?</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-97" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-97" data-faq-toggle>
            I have booked a tour but would like to add one or more bicycles to my booking. Is that possible?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-97" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>Unfortunately, we cannot arrange this. However, bicycles can be hired at several locations during Dutch Design Week (DDW). You can also hire an OV-fiets from Eindhoven Central Station or Strijp-S station.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-102" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-102" data-faq-toggle>
            I would like to book more than 10 tours. Can you help me?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-102" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>We would be happy to discuss the options with you. Contact us at <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#96e2f9e3e4e5d6f2e3e2f5fef2f3e5fff1f8f0f9e3f8f2f7e2fff9f8b8f5f9fb" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="80f4eff5f2f3c0e4f5f4e3e8e4e5f3e9e7eee6eff5eee4e1f4e9efeeaee3efed">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-98" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-98" data-faq-toggle>
            When do the tours take place?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-98" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>The tours take place from Saturday 17 to Saturday 24 October inclusive.</p><p>Design Tours can be booked in time slots, with a new slot available every half hour. A limited number of tours is available per time slot.</p><p>If no tours are available in a particular time slot, the maximum number of tours has already been booked for that time. No additional tours can depart due to the availability of the Design Guides.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-99" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-99" data-faq-toggle>
            How long does a tour last?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-99" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>The tours last between 1.5 and 4 hours.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-103" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-103" data-faq-toggle>
            In which languages can I book a tour?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-103" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>Tours are generally offered in Dutch or English. If you would prefer another language, please contact us at <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#3e4a514b4c4d7e5a4b4a5d565a5b4d57595058514b505a5f4a575150105d5153" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="c5b1aab0b7b685a1b0b1a6ada1a0b6aca2aba3aab0aba1a4b1acaaabeba6aaa8">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>. We will see whether it is possible to offer the tour in your preferred language.</p><p></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-105" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-105" data-faq-toggle>
            Some members of my tour group have limited mobility. What should I do?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-105" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>You can let us know when booking your tour. We will then contact you to ensure the tour is accessible for everyone.</p><p>Did you not mention this when booking? Email us at <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#15617a60676655716061767d7170667c727b737a607b7174617c7a7b3b767a78" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="7a0e150f08093a1e0f0e19121e1f09131d141c150f141e1b0e13151454191517">[email&#160;protected]</span></a> to let us know.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-101" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-101" data-faq-toggle>
            Why don’t I receive the Early Bird discount?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-101" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>Early Bird tickets are intended for individual visitors. Tickets purchased by invoice receive a volume discount instead of the Early Bird discount.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-104" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-104" data-faq-toggle>
            Can I use the hired bicycle for the entire day of the tour?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-104" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>Unfortunately not. The bicycle is reserved specifically for you and your group for the duration of the Design Tour.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                            </div>
                        </div>
                                            <div class="mb-10">
                            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Other questions</h2>
                            <div class="divide-y divide-fuchsia-medium">
                                                                    <div id="faq-46" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-46" data-faq-toggle>
            Where can I find first aid?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-46" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>During Dutch Design Week, there is a First Aid post in the Klokgebouw.</p><p>For all other locations, the staff/organisation of the respective location should be informed. They can handle simple First Aid cases themselves or refer you to the right person.</p><p>In case of an emergency, always contact 112.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-47" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-47" data-faq-toggle>
            Where can I go for lost property?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-47" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Found items are kept at the information desk in Klokgebouw. If you have lost something that has not yet been found, please email </span><a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#f5819c969e908186b5918081969d9190869c929b939a809b9194819c9a9bdb969a98" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255); background-color: transparent;"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="5a2e3339313f2e291a3e2f2e39323e3f29333d343c352f343e3b2e33353474393537">[email&#160;protected]</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> with a clear description of the item.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">If your item is found during or after DDW and your contact details are included with it, we will contact you. After DDW, lost property is kept for a maximum of one month.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-29" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-29" data-faq-toggle>
            Are assistance dogs allowed?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-29" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>Dutch Design Week is fully accessible to assistance dogs. The dog must wear a harness that clearly indicates it is an assistance dog.</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-30" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-30" data-faq-toggle>
            Is there a breastfeeding room?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-30" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p>The <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/place/Klokgebouw,+5651+GW+Eindhoven/@51.4484443,5.4579119,17z/data=!4m6!3m5!1s0x47c6d96b3a220f6b:0x3a0eb3741c513904!8m2!3d51.4486013!4d5.4569803!16s%2Fg%2F11gy0937t2?entry=ttu&amp;g_ep=EgoyMDI0MDkyNS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Klokgebouw</a> has a breastfeeding room. If you&#39;d like to use it, please visit the information desk in the entrance hall (Klokgebouw 50).</p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                                    <div id="faq-70" class="p-4 transition">
    <h3 class="text-lg">
        <button type="button" class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-left"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-70" data-faq-toggle>
            What can I do if I cannot wear my wristband for all nine days?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 transition-transform duration-200 transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </h3>
    <div id="faq-answer-70" class="faq-answer overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"
        style="height: 0;" hidden>
        <p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">If you are unable to wear your wristband throughout DDW because of work, a hospital stay or another important reason, you can request a personal pass at the service desk in Klokgebouw or at Eindhoven Central Station. This pass will replace your wristband for the remainder of DDW.</span></p><p><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Please not</strong><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">e: You can only request a pass while your wristband is still secured around your wrist. First exchange your e-ticket for a wristband and then submit your request. Always have your wristband removed by a member of the service team. If you cut it off yourself, it will no longer be valid and a personal pass cannot be issued.</span></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Requests for a personal pass are assessed on a case-by-case basis. Unfortunately, we cannot accommodate every request; the decision of the service team is final.</span></p>
    </div>
</div>
                                                            </div>
                        </div>
                                    </div>
                    </div>
    </div>
